---
import Layout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Jeff Wieland">
  <article>
  <h1>
        Senior Director of Product Management<br />
        <span style="color: var(--muted)">
          Platform & Ecosystem
        </span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-tagline">
  Director-level product leader building scalable, privacy-aware platforms for
  real-time marketplaces and data-driven ecosystems.
</p>
  <section id="stats" style="background-color: #1a1a1a; color: white; padding: 4rem 0; text-align: center;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-around; flex-wrap: wrap; max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; gap: 2rem;">
        
        <div class="stat-box">
          <h2 class="stat" data-target="18">0</h2>
          <p>Years in AdTech</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="stat-box">
          <h2 class="stat" data-target="8">0</h2>
          <p>Years in Product Management</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="stat-box">
          <h2 class="stat" data-target="300000">0</h2>
          <p>Systems Throughput (QPS)</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="stat-box">
          <h2 class="stat" data-target="25">0</h2>
          <p>Commits on Prebid.org</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <style>
      .stat-box {
        flex: 1 1 200px;
        background: #2c2c2c;
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 2rem 1rem;
        transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
      }

      .stat-box:hover {
        transform: translateY(-5px);
        box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
      }

      .stat {
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        color: #4fd1c5; /* accent color */
        font-weight: bold;
      }

      .stat-box p {
        margin: 0;
        color: #ccc;
        font-size: 1rem;
      }
    </style>

    <script>
      // Animate numbers when section comes into view
      const stats = document.querySelectorAll('.stat');
      const options = { threshold: 0.5 };
      
      const animateStat = (stat) => {
        const target = +stat.getAttribute('data-target');
        let count = 0;
        const increment = target / 100; // adjust speed

        const update = () => {
          count += increment;
          if(count < target){
            stat.textContent = Math.floor(count).toLocaleString();
            requestAnimationFrame(update);
          } else {
            stat.textContent = target.toLocaleString();
          }
        }
        update();
      }

      const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries, obs) => {
        entries.forEach(entry => {
          if(entry.isIntersecting){
            animateStat(entry.target);
            obs.unobserve(entry.target);
          }
        });
      }, options);

      stats.forEach(stat => observer.observe(stat));
    </script>
    <section>
      <h2>Strategy & Leadership</h2>      
      <p>
        I’m a product leader with a track record of defining strategy, shaping roadmaps, and delivering high-impact products at scale. Over the past decade, I’ve guided cross-functional teams through complex platform and data initiatives that power business growth and improve user experiences for millions of users.</br></br>

        I thrive at the intersection of <strong>vision and execution</strong>—partnering with engineering, design, data, and business stakeholders to set priorities, align on strategy, and ensure measurable outcomes. My work focuses on building <strong>scalable platforms</strong>, enabling ecosystem growth, and turning data into actionable insights that drive engagement and business impact.</br></br>

        Beyond day-to-day product leadership, I actively contribute to the broader industry through <strong>public speaking, technical demos, and standards leadership</strong>, helping shape how organizations approach privacy, consent, and data measurement at scale.</br></br>

        I’m seeking opportunities to lead <strong>product strategy at the Sr. director level</strong>, influencing not just individual products, but the broader platform and organizational direction.</br></br>
      </p>
      
      <h1>How I Operate as a Principal Technical Product Manager</h1>
      <h2>1. I start with company-scale problems, not features</h2>
      <p>I focus on problems that materially impact revenue, platform leverage, or long-term competitiveness. I look for multi-year structural constraints—latency ceilings, ecosystem misalignment, regulatory risk, or GTM bottlenecks—and frame them in a way that enables executive alignment and sustained investment.</p>

      <h2>2. I operate at the intersection of platform, GTM, and ecosystem</h2>
      <p>The most valuable product work in AdTech happens between organizations, not within a single team. I routinely work across engineering, sales, partnerships, legal, and external stakeholders to ensure platforms are technically sound, commercially viable, and adoptable at ecosystem scale.</p>

      <h2>3. I lead through influence and clarity</h2>
      <p>At Senior Director scope, progress depends less on authority and more on clarity. I invest heavily in:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Clear problem framing and written narratives</li>
        <li>Explicit trade-offs and decision criteria</li>
        <li>Metrics that reflect both system health and business outcomes</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This creates alignment across senior engineering leaders, GTM teams, and executives.</p>

      <h2>4. I treat scale, latency, and reliability as first-class product features</h2>
      <p>In real-time advertising systems, performance is the product. I partner deeply with engineering to understand system limits, define success thresholds, and ensure that growth does not compromise auction health, buyer outcomes, or publisher revenue.</p>

      <h2>5. I build platforms that outlive individual roadmaps</h2>
      <p>My goal is to leave behind durable platforms, not isolated launches. That means:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Designing for extensibility and future use cases</li>
        <li>Avoiding customer-specific dead ends</li>
        <li>Ensuring ownership models that scale across teams and years</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. I represent the company externally when it matters</h2>
      <p>When appropriate, I engage directly in industry forums, standards bodies, and open-source communities. This builds trust, accelerates adoption, and ensures that platform strategy aligns with where the ecosystem is actually going.</p>
  
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

